That was close to death; the first hit of a green slime got through and
I had nothing in my inventory to fix it, nor quick teleport to the upper
levels to pray. Killed the slime on the first move. Looked into my bag
of holding and found two wands of fire, took them both out. On the third
move zapped one the wands... nothing happens. On the fourth move I zapped
the second wand... nothing happens. On the next move I fetched my wand of
wishing. On the sixth move I wished for a wand of fire. At that moment I
got the "You are turning into green slime." message; what a horror! But
I still have one move... I zap myself with the wand... What a relief!!!

The problems were the unidentified wands; then I was burdened; after
taking out the third wand (the WoW) from my bag I got stressed; so I
made the mistake to not drop the bag in the very first move; then I did
not have cursed scrolls of teleport available (which might not have
helped since I had no teleport control). Shame on me, so many mistakes!

Ah, another one; I had got a throne genocide and completely forgot about
the green slimes; that would have been a perfect genocide choice. Well,
the RNG exploits every weakness.

On the plus side, I had my WoW recharged (and I usually don't do that).

The irony... After I turned around the second corner an elf lord - you
know what's coming? - zapped a wand of fire on me! (The RNG is cruel.)

Being superstitious one might puzzle about why the sliming did happen
*exactly* (no joke[*]) at T:42000; a 1000 times "42"?! Strange.

Janis

[*] ttyrec file available at NAO.

And another strange thing with this game as a PS:

I had a tame (red colored) marilith and got two additional large dogs.
Both dogs died after the above event quite at the same time but not in
the same maze region. I quickly found the corpses and turned them again
to life. I thought, these dogs seem quite wimpy, I'll go and polymorph
them; I lined them up in a row, zapped, and got... - a tame balrog and
a tame barbed devil. Now I have three different red & as pets. What a
strange coincidence, this too. Halloween is bygone, isn't it?


